flowchart TD
  flags[Command-line flags]
  env[Environment variables]
  keyfiles[Key files]
  air[Air-gapped guard]
  probe[Connectivity probe]
  providers[Provider registry]
  gguf[Local GGUF model]
  llmrunner[LLM runner]
  runners[Chat and Overview runners]
  serverllm[GUI server's own client]
  cloud[Cloud endpoints]
  bind[GUI bind address]
  outside[Outside the guard]

  flags -->|air-gapped flag, opt-in| air
  air -->|deletes env keys only| env
  air -->|startup check| probe
  env -->|API keys| providers
  keyfiles -->|API keys, not scrubbed| providers
  providers -->|cloud descriptor| llmrunner
  flags -->|names a model| llmrunner
  gguf -->|path from flags| llmrunner
  llmrunner -->|cloud calls| cloud
  runners -->|cloud calls| cloud
  serverllm -->|cloud calls| cloud
  air -->|guards each caller| llmrunner
  air -->|guards each caller| runners
  air -->|guards each caller| serverllm
  flags -->|host flag, server.js only| bind
  air -->|refuses non-loopback| bind
  air -->|does not reach| outside

%% tip: Air-gapped guard :: Opt-in. Blocks CodeExam's own cloud AI calls. It is not a network sandbox.
%% tip: air-gapped flag, opt-in :: Nothing is guarded unless the flag is given. Typed with an underscore to node src/server.js directly, it is silently ignored.
%% tip: Connectivity probe :: One TCP connect to api.anthropic.com at startup. A clean result does not prove isolation.
%% tip: Outside the guard :: The standalone MCP server, images in rendered chat answers, and what you save.
